  <h2 id="introduction">1. Introduction</h2>
  <p>MasakaMart is an online marketplace for groceries, fresh food, and everyday household essentials. These Terms and Conditions apply when you browse the website, create an account, submit an order, or otherwise use MasakaMart services. By placing an order, you confirm that you have read these terms and accept them for that transaction. The Privacy Policy, Delivery Policy, and Returns &amp; Refunds Policy form part of the information provided to customers and should be read alongside these terms.</p>

  <h2 id="definitions">2. Definitions</h2>
  <p>“MasakaMart”, “we”, “us”, and “our” mean the MasakaMart service and its administrators. “Customer” or “you” means a person using the website or placing an order. “Product” means an item listed for sale. “Order” means a request submitted through checkout. “Payment” means money tendered or a payment request made for an order. “Delivery” means fulfilment to the location supplied by the customer. “Pickup” means collection from the pickup location shown at checkout.</p>

  <h2 id="eligibility">3. Eligibility and account registration</h2>
  <p>You must provide truthful, current information when registering and ordering, including your name, email address, and phone number. Keep your password confidential and tell MasakaMart promptly through the support channel if you suspect unauthorized access. Do not impersonate another person, create accounts for fraud, or use another customer’s account without permission. Account recovery and profile updates are available through the existing account flows. We may investigate suspected misuse and apply proportionate protective restrictions, while considering information provided by the affected customer.</p>

  <h2 id="products">4. Product information and availability</h2>
  <p>We aim to keep product names, descriptions, images, prices, discounts, and stock information accurate. Fresh and market goods may vary slightly in appearance, size, or availability, and an image may be illustrative. Stock is checked again during checkout and before the order is committed. If an item becomes unavailable or a genuine listing error is identified, we will explain the issue and may remove the affected item, cancel the affected order, or arrange an appropriate replacement or refund through support. We do not use these terms to create false scarcity or misleading discounts.</p>

  <h2 id="prices">5. Prices, discounts, and charges</h2>
  <p>Prices are shown in Ugandan Shillings (UGX). The checkout summary shows the item subtotal, applicable discounts, delivery fee, and total before submission. Delivery fees come from the active delivery zone or the server-side location quote. We do not intentionally add undisclosed charges. A genuine pricing or configuration error may be corrected before fulfilment; where a customer has already paid and the order cannot fairly be fulfilled at the displayed terms, support will explain the available remedy.</p>

  <h2 id="orders">6. Placing and confirming orders</h2>
  <p>To order, review the cart, provide customer and fulfilment details, select delivery or pickup, select an available payment method, review the total, accept these terms, and submit checkout. The system revalidates stock, delivery eligibility, and totals on the server. An order may first show as received with payment pending; this is not proof that payment has been received. Order status and payment status are separate and may be viewed through the order pages. Duplicate submissions or technical errors should be reported to support with the order number; cancellation does not erase the order or payment history.</p>

  <h2 id="payments">7. Payment terms</h2>
  <p>The checkout currently presents Mobile Money through PesaJet, cash on delivery, and a card option. A Mobile Money prompt or payment request is not the same as confirmed receipt. Payment is treated as paid only after the applicable provider verification, callback, or authorized review records a successful result. Delayed, failed, expired, cancelled, duplicate, or disputed payments may remain pending while they are investigated. Authorized administrators may review or update payment status under the application’s permission and audit controls; a manual status change does not remove the underlying transaction history. MasakaMart does not request a customer’s Mobile Money PIN.</p>

  <h2 id="delivery">8. Delivery and pickup</h2>
  <p>Customers may choose delivery where the service is enabled and the location is within an active service area, or pickup where an active pickup location is available. The applicable delivery fee is shown before order submission and recalculated on the server. Location details should be accurate and may be supplied by delivery zone or by a location search. Delivery estimates depend on order volume, stock, traffic, weather, and service-provider availability and are not guarantees. If a customer is unavailable or the address is inaccurate, contact support to discuss a reasonable reschedule or other available arrangement. Pickup instructions and location details shown at checkout apply to that order.</p>

  <h2 id="cancellation">9. Order cancellation</h2>
  <p>Contact MasakaMart through the support channel as soon as possible to request cancellation. A request may be easier to accommodate before preparation or dispatch begins, but it is not guaranteed after fulfilment work has started. Cancellation will not silently delete order or payment records. Any payment or stock adjustment will be handled according to the order’s actual status, provider result, and applicable Returns &amp; Refunds Policy. A customer should not treat a payment request as cancelled merely because the checkout page was closed.</p>

  <h2 id="returns">10. Returns, defective products, and refunds</h2>
  <p>For an item that is damaged, spoiled, incorrect, missing, or materially different from the order, contact support with the order number and relevant details as soon as reasonably possible. The current Returns &amp; Refunds Policy asks customers to report affected items within 24 hours of delivery; this operational rule does not remove any rights that cannot lawfully be excluded. Fresh, perishable, and hygiene-sensitive goods may require special handling. MasakaMart may offer a replacement, refund, or another appropriate remedy after review. Approved refunds are arranged through the original Mobile Money number or store credit where applicable; a refund request is not the same as a processed refund, and timing depends on verification and the payment provider. No automatic refund is promised where the system has not confirmed one.</p>

  <h2 id="responsibilities">11. Customer responsibilities and acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Customers must provide accurate contact, payment, and delivery information, keep accounts secure, and inspect deliveries reasonably promptly. You must not use the website for fraud, unauthorized access, payment manipulation, abusive conduct, deliberate exploitation of errors, or interference with another customer’s use. These rules do not prevent honest complaints, good-faith payment disputes, lawful reviews, or requests for assistance.</p>

  <h2 id="privacy">12. Privacy and personal information</h2>
  <p>MasakaMart uses information such as name, phone number, email address, delivery details, order history, support information, and payment references to process orders, communicate status, support delivery and pickup, prevent fraud, and maintain the service. Analytics are used only where the site’s consent mechanism permits them. PesaJet processes Mobile Money transactions, and MasakaMart does not receive or store a Mobile Money PIN. See the Privacy Policy for information about access, correction, deletion requests, security, and cookies. Accepting these terms does not authorize unlimited marketing, sale, or disclosure of personal information.</p>

  <h2 id="security">13. Website security and availability</h2>
  <p>MasakaMart uses reasonable technical and operational measures to protect accounts, orders, and payment information, but no online service can promise uninterrupted availability or perfect security. Maintenance, network failures, payment-provider outages, geocoding failures, and other events may temporarily affect the website. We may investigate suspicious activity and temporarily restrict an account, order, or payment where necessary to protect customers or the service. Restrictions should be proportionate and reviewed when the relevant information is available.</p>

  <h2 id="intellectual-property">14. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>MasakaMart’s branding, website design, software, original text, and original graphics are protected by applicable intellectual-property rights. You may use the website for personal, lawful shopping and may not copy, scrape, reverse engineer, republish, or misuse protected material except as permitted by law. Product names, supplier material, and third-party photographs may belong to their respective owners; these terms do not transfer those rights to MasakaMart.</p>

  <h2 id="third-party-services">15. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>MasakaMart relies on third-party services for Mobile Money processing through PesaJet, email delivery, analytics where consented, geocoding or location services, and communication links where enabled. Their availability and processing are subject to their own systems and terms. MasakaMart remains responsible for handling its own order workflow and will not treat a third-party interruption as proof that a payment succeeded or failed without appropriate verification.</p>

  <h2 id="liability">16. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>MasakaMart is not responsible for loss caused solely by information supplied incorrectly by a customer, unauthorized use of a customer’s credentials, or events outside reasonable control. Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability for fraud, deliberate misconduct, or any responsibility that cannot lawfully be excluded, and statutory consumer protections remain applicable. Any limitation should be interpreted reasonably and proportionately to the service and the actual loss.</p>

  <h2 id="complaints">17. Complaints and dispute resolution</h2>
  <p>Customers should submit product, payment, delivery, refund, or account complaints through the existing support channel and include the order number, a description of the issue, and relevant evidence such as photographs or transaction references. MasakaMart will review the available records and respond through the contact details associated with the account or order. Customers may request clarification or escalation and may use any lawful consumer, regulatory, or court process available to them. No complaint process in these terms removes a customer’s legal rights.</p>

  <h2 id="changes">18. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>MasakaMart may update these terms to reflect service, legal, security, or operational changes. The effective date and last-updated date will identify the published version. Material changes should be communicated through an appropriate website, account, or service notice and should not retroactively change the terms of completed transactions or remove established rights. A new order after the effective date may require acceptance of the updated version.</p>

  <h2 id="suspension">19. Suspension and termination</h2>
  <p>MasakaMart may suspend or close access where necessary for fraud prevention, security, legal compliance, or serious misuse. Except where urgent action is needed, we should consider the customer’s explanation and the effect on pending orders, payments, refunds, and complaints. Suspension does not cancel payment records, erase order history, or remove rights relating to an existing transaction. Customers may contact support to request review of a restriction.</p>

  <h2 id="governing-law">20. Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are intended to operate in connection with MasakaMart’s services in Uganda. The choice of Ugandan law, the appropriate courts, and any mandatory consumer or electronic-commerce requirements should be confirmed by a qualified Ugandan legal professional before publication.</p>

  <h2 id="severability">21. Severability and interpretation</h2>
  <p>If a provision is found unenforceable, it should be read down or severed only to the extent necessary, while the remaining provisions continue where lawful. Headings are for navigation and do not limit the meaning of a section. If these terms conflict with a mandatory legal right or a specific written order remedy, the mandatory right or specific remedy prevails to the extent required.</p>

  <h2 id="communications">22. Electronic communications</h2>
  <p>Customers agree that MasakaMart may communicate about accounts, orders, payments, delivery, pickup, support, and security through the email address, phone number, website notices, or in-app notifications associated with the account. Electronic records, timestamps, order status changes, and payment-provider responses may be used to administer the service, subject to applicable law and the Privacy Policy. Customers should keep contact details current and check messages relating to active orders.</p>

  <h2 id="contact">23. Contact and customer support</h2>
  <p>For questions, complaints, delivery issues, returns, refunds, or payment investigations, use the Contact / Support area linked in the website footer and account area. Include your order number and enough information for MasakaMart to locate the relevant record. The website’s published support route is the authoritative contact method; no unverified email address, telephone number, registered business name, licence, or physical address is added by these terms.</p>

  <h2 id="final-statement">24. Final statement</h2>
  <p>These terms are intended to make MasakaMart’s current shopping, payment, fulfilment, support, and information practices understandable and fair. They should be read with the Privacy Policy, Delivery Policy, and Returns &amp; Refunds Policy. The published version is dated <?= e($termsVersion) ?> and remains subject to appropriate operational review and qualified Ugandan legal review before being treated as final legal advice.</p>
